YaCy on FenrirOS
================

YaCy is a peer-to-peer web search engine: it crawls pages for its own index and
shares index fragments with other peers. Nothing is enabled or started for you.

  yacy                              runs it in the foreground as yourself (data: ~/yacy-data)
  /etc/dinit.d/yacy                 the service (dinitctl enable yacy): runs as _yacy, data in /var/lib/yacy/yacy-data
  http://localhost:8090/            the web interface (the administration pages need no password
                                    from this machine: adminAccountForLocalhost is on in YaCy's defaults;
                                    set an administrator password under Administration before opening it up)

YaCy joins the public freeworld network as soon as it starts, and then talks to other
peers and crawls what you tell it to crawl: start it only where that is wanted. Memory
use is set in the data directory's settings (Performance pages), 600 MB by default.
